# PROJECT: FanStore - Film & TV Series Merchandise E-Commerce
# FRAMEWORK: Laravel 11 (PHP 8.2+)
# DATABASE: MySQL
# FRONTEND: Bootstrap 5.3 + AdminLTE 3 (modular CSS from dist/css/alt/)

## CODING RULES
- Always use Laravel 11 syntax (bootstrap/app.php middleware, NOT Kernel.php)
- Never use env() directly in code — always use config() helper
- All middleware registered via withMiddleware() in bootstrap/app.php
- Use Bootstrap 5.3 data attributes: data-bs-toggle, data-bs-dismiss (NOT data-toggle)
- AdminLTE: use modular CSS files from dist/css/alt/ to avoid Bootstrap conflicts
- All API keys stored in .env and mapped through config/services.php
- Images: always use Intervention Image v3 (intervention/image-laravel)
- Image storage: Storage::disk('public')->put(path, (string)$encoded)
- File uploads: validate with File::image() NOT just mimes rule
- TMDB API: use Bearer Token in Authorization header (NOT api_key query param)
- TMDB TV shows use 'name' field (NOT 'title') — movies use 'title'
- Google Maps: use new PlaceAutocompleteElement API with gmp-select event
- Always use UUID for uploaded file names (Str::uuid()->toString())
- Order tracking states (enum): sourcing, packaging, shipped, on_the_way, delivered
- Balance logic: always deduct from user balance first, then charge card for remainder
- Cancelled orders: refund goes to user balance (NOT credit card), log in transactions table
- AppServiceProvider: add URL::forceScheme('https') for production
- All Blade forms must have @csrf
- Admin routes protected by 'admin' middleware alias
- Use soft deletes where appropriate
- All controllers use Form Request classes for validation
- Database: follow 3NF normalization

## FOLDER STRUCTURE RULES
- Services in app/Services/ (TMDBService, WeatherService, MapsService)
- Form Requests in app/Http/Requests/
- Admin controllers in app/Http/Controllers/Admin/
- User controllers in app/Http/Controllers/User/

## DEPLOYMENT (Railway.app)
- nixpacks.toml must set NIXPACKS_PHP_ROOT_DIR = '/app/public'
- Volume mount path: /app/storage
- LOG_CHANNEL=stderr in production
- Never hardcode credentials

## DO NOT
- Never use Kernel.php (removed in Laravel 11)
- Never use data-toggle (Bootstrap 4, use data-bs-toggle)
- Never use ml-*, mr-*, pl-*, pr-* Bootstrap classes (use ms-*, me-*, ps-*, pe-*)
- Never call env() outside of config files
- Never store uploaded files with original filenames
- Never skip server-side validation
- Never put API keys in frontend JS directly (use Blade + config())
